WEBVTT

00:06.010 --> 00:07.410
Good morning!

00:06.770 --> 00:07.980
Oh, morning.

00:13.140 --> 00:15.450
<i>A masterful cat starts his mornings early.</i>

00:25.790 --> 00:27.120
<i>The reason...</i>

00:46.630 --> 00:50.610
<i>My owner's daily lunch box, 
the masterful cat special.</i>

00:47.270 --> 00:51.780
* Grilled Salmon
 * Egg Omelet
 * Burdock Root and Carrots
 * Hearty Pork Soup

00:54.210 --> 00:58.280
<i>My worthless human owner's 
lunch must be made.</i>

00:59.390 --> 01:03.280
<i>Once again, from the moment I open 
my eyes, I am a masterful cat.</i>

01:06.330 --> 01:08.660
<i>Compared to me, this...</i>

01:12.380 --> 01:15.090
I can't go to work today.

01:12.590 --> 01:17.930
<b>Gloom</b>

01:14.090 --> 01:17.930
<b>Gloom</b>

01:15.090 --> 01:17.530
My covers won't let me go.

01:19.140 --> 01:20.930
<i>...human of mine is worthless!</i>

01:24.210 --> 01:25.560
Hot!

01:25.560 --> 01:28.480
Hot! Hot! Hot!

01:28.480 --> 01:30.670
How can you be so inhuman!

01:31.510 --> 01:32.570
<i>I am a cat.</i>

01:34.670 --> 01:36.920
<i>However, I must persevere.</i>

01:36.920 --> 01:38.320
<i>Everything I do...</i>

01:38.740 --> 01:42.330
<b>Cat Dash</b>

01:40.240 --> 01:42.330
<i>is for the sake of the cat can!</i>

01:40.370 --> 01:42.330
Is for the sake...

01:40.370 --> 01:42.330
...of the cat can
(living expenses)!!

01:44.060 --> 01:47.300
Yukichi, you're really such a masterful cat!

01:44.370 --> 01:48.790
Her eyes are
 wide awake now

01:47.300 --> 01:48.790
So good!

01:49.420 --> 01:51.320
This is true happiness!

01:52.120 --> 01:54.800
<i>Of course. Of course. I need you...</i>

01:55.470 --> 01:58.360
<i>To stay healthy and work hard today...</i>

01:59.010 --> 02:01.530
I'm so happy that...

02:01.530 --> 02:03.740
I want to take a day off work!

02:03.600 --> 02:05.020
<i>What did you say?!</i>

02:05.020 --> 02:10.520
<b>Rub Rub</b>

02:05.340 --> 02:10.520
I want to stay at home all day! 
I want to rub Yukichi's belly!

02:10.520 --> 02:13.070
<b>Alarm</b>

02:13.070 --> 02:19.070
<b>Twitch</b>

02:13.070 --> 02:19.070
<b>Twitch</b>

02:14.260 --> 02:16.340
It's already time!

02:16.900 --> 02:18.150
<i>This human...</i>

02:18.150 --> 02:19.920
<i>Isn't this human...</i>

02:19.920 --> 02:23.580
<i>finally reaching the point 
of total hopelessness?</i>

02:24.450 --> 02:29.510
<i>Maybe I should toss this human aside 
and find a new place to live.</i>

02:30.210 --> 02:31.740
Oh, Yukichi!

02:32.590 --> 02:36.920
Today's pay day, so we should 
do <i>that</i> when I get home! <i>That</i>!

02:40.210 --> 02:43.290
C-h-e-e-r-s.

02:45.470 --> 02:47.320
Cheers!

02:51.570 --> 02:53.200
I'm off!

03:01.930 --> 03:03.990
<i>Well, I guess it won't hurt...</i>

03:04.910 --> 03:07.530
<i>to wait here a bit longer.</i>

03:09.030 --> 03:11.480
<i>An out-of-service train will be passing by.</i>

03:28.640 --> 03:29.980
<i>Anger!</i>

03:45.870 --> 03:50.750
<b>The Masterful Cat
Is Depressed Again Today</b>

04:59.940 --> 05:03.610
Can

04:59.940 --> 05:03.610
<b>A Masterful Cat Also Cares about Health</b>

05:03.740 --> 05:04.950
<b>A Masterful Cat Also Cares about Health</b>

05:03.820 --> 05:04.950
Can

05:11.900 --> 05:15.580
As always, the food Yukichi 
cooks is the best!

05:15.580 --> 05:16.870
Yukichi!

05:17.620 --> 05:21.130
Is there any more of 
this wasabi potato salad?

05:21.580 --> 05:26.510
Oh, I'd love some more hot sake, too!

05:28.870 --> 05:30.760
Thanks!

05:31.600 --> 05:33.770
My own home is the best!

05:34.020 --> 05:34.770
Snap

05:41.510 --> 05:43.530
Huh? What?

05:44.010 --> 05:46.470
Didn't I hook the clasp properly?!

05:47.480 --> 05:49.900
Maybe it's time to buy 
some new work clothes...

05:52.360 --> 05:53.440
No!

05:52.370 --> 05:55.750
<b>Thump</b>

05:53.440 --> 05:55.490
No! No! No! Hold on! Hold on!

05:55.490 --> 05:58.750
Not now! Definitely not right now!

06:08.760 --> 06:14.140
<b>Depressed...</b>

06:10.200 --> 06:14.140
Why are you more shocked than me?

06:14.140 --> 06:17.640
Wait! Hold on! Don't be so hasty!

06:14.870 --> 06:15.900
<i>Withdrawn!</i>

06:18.120 --> 06:20.420
Exercise! I'll lose the weight with exercise!

06:20.420 --> 06:23.190
My sake and snacks!

06:23.520 --> 06:25.530
<i>Currently adjusting her clasp.</i>

06:25.530 --> 06:31.220
I'm sure I gained weight from all 
the work outings and our company trip!

06:31.120 --> 06:32.990
<b>Right?</b>

06:31.220 --> 06:36.190
It'll go right back down as long as 
I use the stairs or do some fast walking.

06:33.370 --> 06:35.990
<b>Right?</b>

06:36.190 --> 06:37.120
Right?

06:37.120 --> 06:39.720
Right? Right? Right?!

06:39.720 --> 06:41.630
It'll be fine!

06:41.630 --> 06:43.790
So, please!

06:43.790 --> 06:49.970
Give it back! If I can't enjoy my 
dinner and evening drink, I—

06:50.460 --> 06:55.460
What's the point of working 
so hard day after day?

07:00.840 --> 07:04.130
Starting tomorrow, 
I'll start an exercise regimen!

07:04.130 --> 07:05.480
Turn off the light.

07:08.570 --> 07:11.990
<i>First of all, I'll wake up thirty 
minutes early and walk to the station.</i>

07:12.480 --> 07:15.130
<i>Maybe I should wear sneakers.</i>

07:16.670 --> 07:20.590
<i>I'll carry some mineral water 
with me and then...</i>

07:20.590 --> 07:24.370
<i>How many calories does 
walking thirty minutes burn?!</i>

07:24.370 --> 07:26.590
<i>Hm? What are diet shoes?</i>

07:27.130 --> 07:30.070
<i>You can burn more calories 
just by wearing them?!</i>

07:30.070 --> 07:32.900
<i>How perfect is that! I'll buy a pair!</i>

07:44.880 --> 07:46.810
I overslept!

07:46.810 --> 07:48.070
Taxi!

08:02.660 --> 08:04.230
<i>I barely made it.</i>

08:04.230 --> 08:07.170
<i>Looks like early morning 
exercise isn't for me.</i>

08:14.650 --> 08:17.350
Oh, there she is! Fukuzawa-san!

08:18.580 --> 08:23.090
Thank you so much for helping me prepare 
the documents until the last train!

08:23.960 --> 08:27.950
Thank you for taking 
my work while I was off!

08:27.950 --> 08:29.150
Me, too! Me, too!

08:29.150 --> 08:32.790
These are some popular local 
sweets from my hometown.

08:33.060 --> 08:35.030
This is from my Guam trip!

08:35.640 --> 08:37.780
Oh! Me, too!

08:40.790 --> 08:42.750
<b>Huge Pile</b>

08:41.240 --> 08:43.910
Well, since they're gifts...

08:44.400 --> 08:47.250
I shouldn't let them go to waste!

08:48.970 --> 08:49.880
<i>She!</i>

08:51.300 --> 08:52.310
<i>Got!</i>

08:53.840 --> 08:54.910
<i>Heavier!</i>

08:56.760 --> 08:58.220
<i>She got heavier.</i>

08:56.760 --> 08:58.220
Huh?

08:58.680 --> 09:02.140
That's so weird. How'd this happen?

09:03.320 --> 09:07.400
Wait! Hold on! Not that! I'll die!

09:17.040 --> 09:20.120
Cold! Cold! Cold! Cold!

09:20.740 --> 09:23.600
I'm really gonna die!

09:23.600 --> 09:27.980
And when did you learn to ride a bicycle?!

09:29.550 --> 09:31.110
<i>One month later.</i>

09:33.210 --> 09:35.450
I've gone down 600 grams!

09:33.210 --> 09:36.170
In order to maintain privacy,
 certain parts of the image have been altered.

09:36.790 --> 09:40.680
It's all thanks to you watching over 
my nightly jogging and muscle training!

09:40.680 --> 09:44.430
At this rate, I can continue losing weight 
slowly without limiting my food intake.

09:47.700 --> 09:49.770
I shouldn't take it slow!

09:48.230 --> 09:49.770
* Yukichi

09:49.770 --> 09:52.110
That's not cute at all!

09:52.760 --> 09:56.110
<i>I immediately limited my 
alcohol and food intake.</i>

09:56.110 --> 09:58.930
<i>I returned to my regular weight in one week.</i>

09:59.610 --> 10:01.910
<i>Yukichi's form went back to normal, too.</i>

10:02.330 --> 10:08.500
<b>Rub Rub</b>

10:03.010 --> 10:06.680
Thank goodness. Thank goodness.

10:04.660 --> 10:08.500
He actually liked it a bit

10:18.570 --> 10:20.100
So cold.

10:20.100 --> 10:21.390
I'm home!

10:21.710 --> 10:23.200
Huh? Yuri?

10:23.200 --> 10:27.270
You should tell me if you're 
planning to come home for a visit!

10:27.270 --> 10:30.020
There's nothing left here for you to eat.

10:30.020 --> 10:31.810
I don't need any food.

10:31.810 --> 10:34.690
I just came by to hand over your 
souvenirs from my company trip.

10:34.690 --> 10:36.690
Oh, a company trip!

10:36.690 --> 10:39.570
It almost sounds like you're a working adult!

10:39.570 --> 10:41.670
I <i>am</i> a working adult.

10:41.670 --> 10:45.650
There's a souvenir from the senpai 
I gave the chigura to, too.

10:45.650 --> 10:46.950
Thanks!

10:48.410 --> 10:50.840
Oh, Yuri-nee. Long time no see!

10:50.840 --> 10:52.670
Oh, Rio! You're here, too!

10:53.120 --> 10:54.410
I'm visiting.

10:54.410 --> 10:56.290
Seeing you in a suit is new.

10:55.300 --> 10:58.170
<b>Cousins</b>

10:56.770 --> 10:58.170
Does it look good on me?

10:58.170 --> 11:00.340
Yeah, you're like a working adult.

11:00.340 --> 11:02.840
I <i>am</i> a working adult.

11:03.250 --> 11:05.770
It's so warm!

11:05.770 --> 11:08.350
Rio, I heard you started living on your own?

11:08.700 --> 11:13.110
Yeah. When Auntie found out, 
she said I could have the TV in your room.

11:13.110 --> 11:14.900
Oh, that thing.

11:14.900 --> 11:17.110
Take it, take it.

11:17.490 --> 11:20.220
Are your hands still full 
with part-time jobs?

11:20.220 --> 11:21.410
Yeah.

11:21.410 --> 11:25.600
To the point that other part-timers 
think of me as a freeter.

11:25.600 --> 11:27.060
You work too much!

11:27.060 --> 11:29.850
You should spend your 
school days falling in love.

11:29.850 --> 11:32.710
You'll barely have any chances 
once you become a working adult.

11:33.210 --> 11:36.710
I thirst for love! You should 
share some love stories with me.

11:37.640 --> 11:39.020
Love stories?!

11:46.510 --> 11:48.230
What the hell are you doing?!

11:48.230 --> 11:49.480
I'm gonna kill you!

11:49.480 --> 11:51.520
Perfect, you've been recorded.

11:53.760 --> 11:55.730
There's someone I'm a little interested in.

11:56.140 --> 11:57.170
Seriously?!

11:57.170 --> 11:58.800
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

11:58.800 --> 12:00.280
What kinda person?!

12:00.280 --> 12:03.480
Well, I forgot to ask for a name...

12:03.480 --> 12:05.780
A customer where you work?!

12:05.780 --> 12:10.540
Yeah, the customer happened to pass by 
when I was arguing with my ex-boyfriend

12:10.540 --> 12:13.170
and saved me.

12:14.120 --> 12:17.920
Maybe some kind of martial artist? 
A really strong one.

12:21.690 --> 12:22.840
What?!

12:22.840 --> 12:25.720
That sounds like a fateful encounter!

12:25.720 --> 12:27.990
Please stop.

12:27.640 --> 12:31.850
Please stop

12:27.800 --> 12:31.850
<b>Po-wa-wan</b>

12:27.990 --> 12:28.820
<i>It's no use!</i>

12:28.310 --> 12:31.850
<b>Ba-dump</b>

12:28.820 --> 12:31.850
<i>I can't help imagining Saku-senpai doing it.</i>

12:31.850 --> 12:33.340
<i>Spot on.</i>

12:33.760 --> 12:36.040
Is this person dating anyone?

12:36.040 --> 12:39.020
I don't think so, but...

12:39.020 --> 12:40.860
There's a roommate.

12:39.020 --> 12:43.030
<b>Sake Brewery Master</b>

12:40.860 --> 12:43.030
<i>An unknown cat.</i>

12:40.860 --> 12:43.030
<b>Heh...</b>

12:43.030 --> 12:44.450
I see.

12:44.450 --> 12:45.660
But that's nice!

12:46.170 --> 12:49.820
A skilled, strong, and 
kind person sounds so nice.

12:49.820 --> 12:51.080
I'm jealous.

12:51.080 --> 12:53.900
Yuri-nee, are you currently single?

12:53.900 --> 12:55.870
I have been for years.

12:55.870 --> 12:57.830
I have bad luck with men.

12:59.260 --> 13:01.640
I can't find any good ones.

13:01.640 --> 13:02.340
Yeah.

13:02.340 --> 13:07.030
I'm starting to think I should look 
for someone of the same sex.

13:07.030 --> 13:08.350
It's so hard to get married.

13:10.020 --> 13:15.060
<i>Is it okay to say I was 
thinking the same thing here?</i>

13:15.620 --> 13:19.020
<i>No, I'm sure the atmosphere'll 
get weird. I shouldn't...</i>

13:19.850 --> 13:21.920
Wait, what's with this weird atmosphere?!

13:21.920 --> 13:22.980
Don't shrink away from me!

13:22.980 --> 13:25.030
I'm still in the joking phase for now!

13:25.030 --> 13:27.390
N-No, I wasn't shrinking away from you!

13:27.390 --> 13:30.450
I w-was just thinking that you 
have a flexible way of thinking!

13:30.450 --> 13:32.090
Really?

13:32.090 --> 13:35.460
Well, you should try to find someone 
before you wind up like me.

13:36.680 --> 13:39.960
Yeah. I have no idea what'll happen,

13:41.290 --> 13:45.970
but I want to give a proper thanks 
the next time we meet

13:45.970 --> 13:48.600
and actually get a name this time.

13:49.590 --> 13:51.330
That's the spirit!

13:51.330 --> 13:53.370
Tell me if anything happens!

13:53.370 --> 13:54.350
Sure thing.

13:54.840 --> 13:58.630
<i>But the cat is usually the one 
who shops where I work.</i>

13:58.630 --> 14:00.360
<i>I'll just have to bide my time and wait.</i>

14:01.350 --> 14:03.360
<i>I should ask for more shifts.</i>

14:03.990 --> 14:06.200
<i>Meanwhile, at the Fukuzawa household...</i>

14:10.400 --> 14:11.580
What's going on?!

14:11.990 --> 14:12.490
<b>Achoo</b>

14:12.610 --> 14:14.580
Is Yukichi coming down with a cold, too?!

14:12.830 --> 14:13.580
<b>Hek-choo</b>

14:13.990 --> 14:14.580
<b>Achoo</b>

14:14.240 --> 14:14.580
<b>Achoo</b>

14:15.410 --> 14:17.580
Has she been doing well, lately?

14:19.830 --> 14:24.500
<b>Beep</b>

14:20.370 --> 14:23.620
Why don't you both come 
and shop together sometime?

14:25.400 --> 14:28.840
<i>This train will stop at every station 
until the final destination.</i>

14:42.200 --> 14:43.500
<i>Cat grass.</i>

14:44.980 --> 14:51.530
<i>It is believed that cats eat it to help 
cough up hairballs or increase vitamin intake.</i>

14:51.530 --> 14:55.700
<i>However, there is no detailed explanation 
of why they enjoy its consumption.</i>

14:59.810 --> 15:02.870
<i>There are cats that absolutely love it!</i>

15:02.870 --> 15:05.960
<i>As well as cats that ignore it completely...</i>

15:05.960 --> 15:08.730
<i>Some people believe it's just a 
"favorite food" for certain cats.</i>

15:06.210 --> 15:09.970
<b>Huge Pile</b>

15:12.470 --> 15:14.970
Shake

15:12.870 --> 15:14.040
<i>Drain.</i>

15:15.640 --> 15:17.110
<i>Cat grass salad.</i>

15:17.110 --> 15:19.130
<i>Cat grass: as much as you like.</i>

15:19.130 --> 15:20.420
<i>Seaweed: to taste.</i>

15:20.420 --> 15:21.810
<i>Bonito flakes: to taste.</i>

15:28.570 --> 15:30.610
I have a delivery.

15:37.080 --> 15:38.660
Oh, hello.

15:38.660 --> 15:41.080
Please sign or stamp here!

15:42.670 --> 15:44.690
I'm hungry...

15:46.840 --> 15:49.090
Thank you very much!

15:50.610 --> 15:53.440
Yukichi! What kind of vegetable is this?

15:53.440 --> 15:55.670
It's hard and bitter!

15:55.100 --> 15:57.720
<b>Munch Munch</b>

15:58.060 --> 15:59.680
<b>Slap Slap</b>

16:00.200 --> 16:01.730
Heimlich back slaps!

16:02.180 --> 16:06.020
What?! This salad wasn't for me?!

16:06.440 --> 16:07.270
<b>Glare</b>

16:06.920 --> 16:08.160
Cat grass?!

16:08.160 --> 16:10.470
No wonder it was so hard and bitter!

16:10.470 --> 16:12.280
I was about to spit it out!

16:12.280 --> 16:13.460
Huh?

16:13.460 --> 16:16.780
Is it okay for humans to eat cat grass?

16:17.640 --> 16:21.670
There are a lot of things that people 
eat that are poisonous to cats.

16:23.210 --> 16:25.290
Like onions and chocolate...

16:28.380 --> 16:32.380
<b>Cat grass</b>

16:28.380 --> 16:32.380
What? What's cat grass?! 
Is that the scientific name?

16:32.960 --> 16:35.640
It is the general term 
for grasses cats enjoy eating

16:36.100 --> 16:38.890
and does not refer to 
a specific type of grass?

16:39.300 --> 16:41.140
So, in the end, what is it?!

16:42.430 --> 16:45.150
I think my stomach is starting to hurt.

16:46.400 --> 16:49.430
Wait! Where are you calling?!

16:49.430 --> 16:50.570
No ambulances!

16:51.070 --> 16:54.950
I'm still conscious and 
have no problems walking!

16:55.310 --> 17:00.590
And I can't tell them that my stomach 
hurts because I stupidly ate some cat grass.

17:04.840 --> 17:08.960
Oh, the type of cat grass 
seeds I gave Yukichi-chan?

17:08.960 --> 17:12.590
It's a blend of oat grass and barley grass.

17:12.590 --> 17:16.290
Oh, did you accidentally eat it, Saku-chan?

17:14.590 --> 17:19.600
<b>Insurance Documents
+
Prescription Records</b>

17:16.290 --> 17:17.810
Oh, yes...

17:17.810 --> 17:22.490
It's healthy, but I'm sure it 
tastes terrible when eaten directly.

17:23.910 --> 17:25.100
<i>Afterward...</i>

17:25.100 --> 17:30.110
Sob

17:25.350 --> 17:25.850
<b>Fluster</b>

17:25.560 --> 17:30.110
<i>Her stomach reacted aggressively to 
something she'd never eaten before.</i>

17:26.600 --> 17:27.100
<b>Fluster</b>

17:27.210 --> 17:30.110
I won't eat things 
without asking every again!

17:27.850 --> 17:28.350
<b>Fluster</b>

17:28.480 --> 17:28.940
<b>Fluster</b>

17:29.110 --> 17:29.610
<b>Fluster</b>

17:29.730 --> 17:30.110
<b>Fluster</b>

17:30.110 --> 17:34.310
<i>Yukichi began to use a special plate 
for his own personal use.</i>

17:30.110 --> 17:36.110
Beware of Cat

17:34.310 --> 17:36.110
Where do they sell something like that?!

17:36.580 --> 17:38.220
<i>Dangerous!</i>

17:38.220 --> 17:40.620
<i>Foods poisonous to cats.</i>

17:40.620 --> 17:43.690
<i>Cacao, avocado, grapes, onions,</i>

17:40.660 --> 17:49.960
* Cacao (Chocolate • Cocoa)

17:41.530 --> 17:49.960
* Avocado

17:42.200 --> 17:49.960
* Grapes (Raisins)

17:42.910 --> 17:49.960
* Onion Family
 (Including Yellow Onions)

17:43.690 --> 17:47.950
<i>fresh and dried squid, shellfish, 
caffeine, alcohol, et cetera...</i>

17:43.750 --> 17:49.960
* Squid • Dried Squid

17:44.410 --> 17:49.960
* Shellfish (Abalone • Sazae)

17:45.290 --> 17:49.960
* Caffeine

17:46.040 --> 17:49.960
* Alcohol etc.

17:49.960 --> 17:53.350
Now that I think about it, 
it's crazy how you cook for me.

17:53.350 --> 17:55.150
You're like a fugu blowfish chef!

17:55.470 --> 17:55.970
<b>Heh</b>

17:55.470 --> 17:55.970
Pull

18:04.860 --> 18:09.000
<i>Today marks the first city-wide 
"just like their owner" contest!</i>

18:09.000 --> 18:12.900
<i>The top five pairs walked on the runway while</i>

18:10.230 --> 18:15.940
news: Pet Contest
 "Just Like Their Owner"!?

18:10.230 --> 18:15.940
They were cheered on by the warm laughter of the audience

18:12.900 --> 18:15.940
<i>being cheered by the warm 
laughter of the audience.</i>

18:15.940 --> 18:18.730
<i>Each pair was so alike.</i>

18:18.730 --> 18:22.570
<i>I often hear that pets 
are just like their owners.</i>

18:21.950 --> 18:27.960
<b>Ba-dump</b>

18:21.950 --> 18:27.960
<b>Ba-dump</b>

18:22.570 --> 18:28.410
<i>Do pets become similar to their 
owners or is it the other way around?</i>

